@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] operator-private-custody
Operator commands MUST use only the explicitly supplied private identity, keep
private material out of store paths, arguments and diagnostics, and remove
temporary private identities on exit. Raw tool errors MUST NOT be printed.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] recipient-reconciliation-publication
Reconciliation MUST include every recovery-enabled user and only selected hosts.
Hostless documents MUST explicitly set recoveryOnly to true; recovery-only
documents MUST reject host recipients. Both kinds MUST require a recovery user
and participate in the same check, decrypt and reconciliation operations.
Every changed document MUST receive a new data key. All candidates MUST validate
before publication; preparation failure MUST preserve all originals. Publication
MUST replace regular files atomically and report interrupted partial publication.
